<title>MEXICO: Autlan sees 1997 sales rising by 7.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Autlan sees 1997 sales rising by 7.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales at Mexican mining company, Autlan, could rise by seven percent in dollar terms in 1997 from the year before, a company official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We are speaking of a seven percent in total for sales, in dollar terms,&quot; said Rafal Lozano, director of finance, at a news conference.</p>
<p>According to the company's annual report, sales in 1996 were $128 million, re-expressed in dollars.</p>
